## Security musts (on top of 00-project-core)
- Never open, print or commit secrets: `.env*`, `.railway-secrets.env`, `~/Documents/Softwares/old-consultancy-service-variables-backup-2026-10-08.json`, any `*backup*.json`. Never run `railway variables` in a way that prints its values.
- Never `git add` `docs/prompts/`, env files or backup json. Never use `git add -A` or `git add .`; name each path. Never force-push.
- Never edit, rename or delete an applied migration. A fix goes into a new migration.
- Every new `SECURITY DEFINER` function needs:
  - `SET search_path = public, pg_temp`
  - `REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION … FROM PUBLIC, anon`
  - `GRANT EXECUTE … TO authenticated` only when the app needs it
  - a permission check inside the function (`app_is_admin()` / `app_can_edit(...)`)
- New tables:
  - RLS on, with policies built on the S4 helpers. Never write a `USING (true)` write policy.
  - No `anon` grants unless the data is meant to be public and the migration header says so.
- Never ask for passwords, or write them, in chat, files, logs or reports. Amit types logins himself.
- Client Manak passwords are secrets (encryption approved for S6). Never return them in list queries, logs or the audit log.
- Tests never modify real users, clients or licences. Test data is named `ZZ TEST …` and deleted afterwards.
- **Live DB safety (incident 8 Oct 2026, 19:54–19:58 IST: a migration rollback test on live held exclusive locks for ~4.5 min and took the app down).**
  - NEVER run migration or DDL rollback tests (ALTER/CREATE/DROP, policies, triggers, `BEGIN … ROLLBACK` around a migration) on the live database. Locks are held until ROLLBACK and block every app request.
  - DB tests on live are SELECT-only, or tiny DML in `BEGIN … ROLLBACK` that finishes in seconds (set `lock_timeout` ≤ 3s, `statement_timeout` ≤ 30s).
  - Migration tests run on a local throwaway copy (schema-only dump + small sample data, no password values).
  - `npm run db:migrate` takes brief locks: run it only when nobody is using the app, and migrations set `SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s'`.

## Amit's standing design rules (every session from S6 on)
1. **AI/MCP-ready.** Any AI model or bot must be able to drive every module through the API or MCP, running under the user's own login and permissions.
   - Business rules live in Postgres RPCs or functions endpoints that check permissions from the user's JWT, not only in React.
   - Each feature gets a typed `xxxApi.ts`. Every new RPC or endpoint is added to `docs/agents/api-catalog.md` (an app MCP server is planned).
2. **Responsive and cross-platform.** Every screen must work on Apple, Windows and Android, in Chrome, Safari, Edge and Firefox.
   - Check widths 360, 390, 768 and 1280 px.
   - Tables scroll horizontally or switch to cards; toolbars use `limsToolbarScrollClass`; dialogs fit on a 360 px screen.
   - Touch targets are at least 40 px. No hover-only actions.
3. **Futuristic.** Proactively propose 1–3 small, high-value improvements per session, such as smart defaults, AI assists, bulk actions, keyboard shortcuts or offline-friendly states. Put them in the plan; don't sneak them into code.

